// E(mu, r) = integral f_ss(l, v, n, r) * |n_dot_l| dl, mu = n_dot_v: the white GGX lobes' single-scattering albedo,
// measured by sampleBSDF's own samples
// GGX_ALBEDO: metal on 32 x 32 nodes, rows uniform in r, columns in mu, both 0 to 1
// GGX_GLASS_ALBEDO: glass seen from the side of index 1 (0) or of the material's ior (1), on 16 nodes each of ior from
// 1 to 3, r and mu, transmission included
// Averages: Ebar = 2 * integral E(mu) mu dmu per row
